  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 7 actions (src/actions.js) and 2 boolean feedbacks (src/feedbacks.js), all plain assignments in getActions/getFeedbacks, no runtime generation. Variables and presets are not catalogued.",
    "Protocol: MQTT over WebSocket to ws://<host>/mqtt with the configured username and password (src/index.js initMqtt). Each command publishes a JSON payload to <topic>/<timestamp>. The topic prefix depends on the device mode reported by the device: Session/0/Record and Session/0/Stream/0 in Normal mode, SessionLL/VideoEncoders/0/Record and SessionLL/VideoEncoders/0/Streams/0 in Low-Latency mode (this.prefix, this.data.mode). Recording and streaming actions switch to the Low-Latency prefix at run time; the feedbacks read this.data.recording.state and this.data.streaming.state.",
    "Action setSCTE (Set SCTE 35 Message Settings) and sendSCTE are only usable with firmware v2.23.20250722 or later and a valid license (action description in the source). In setSCTE the properties multidropdown selects which of the other fields are used; the other fields use isVisibleExpression with arrayIncludes($(options:properties), ...), recorded in visibleWhen. The callback only sends fields whose value is truthy, so a value of 0 is not sent. setSCTE always posts to SessionLL/VideoEncoders/0/Metadata/set.",
    "Actions setRecordingName and recordWithName both use the option id command (a file name, despite the id) and post {name} to <record prefix>/RECUpload/set; recordWithName then also posts start. setStreamingInfo posts {password, channel_name, username, url, stream} to <stream prefix>/RTMP/set; its option ids are streamName, username, password, streamURL and streamKey. None of these textinputs has a default or useVariables in the source.",
    "The feedback dropdown values are state strings as reported by the device. The option default of recordingState ('Recording') and streamingState ('Live') match a choice id.",
    "The module manifest runs on node22. Built on @companion-module/base ~1.12.1: options do not support expressions, even though the source uses isVisibleExpression for visibility."
  ]
}
